| How much slower does g77 code run compared to DU fortran?

I have a fortran77-program that simulates non-equilibrium molecular
dynamics, and have compared running times on:

1) PII-266, linux 2.0.34, egcs-g77-1.0.2-8
2) DEC PWS433a, linux 2.0.34, egcs-g77-1.0.3a-2
3) Same as 2), but compiled the program statically under Digital UNIX
   with Digital Fortran 77 V4.0-1-3231 and ran it on the PWS433a.


The running times (calculated by "time ./nemd") was:

1) 108 sec
2)  49 sec
3)  34 sec

It seems that egcs has a lot to catch up with compared with Digital's
own compiler.


