On 26 Jun 1998 11:06:17 GMT, Ewald R. de Wit <ewald@pobox.com> wrote:
:Martin Kahlert wrote:
:>If you mainly work with FFT, the reason for your code running too
:>slow might be the glibc implementation of sin/cos.
:
:Not likely, non-braindead FFT routines don't depend on trig speed.

True, but programs which solve linear equations in the Fourier domain
(a prime use for FFT's) very often need sin/cos in other places---for
example applying frequency domain operators which look like

                 A*e^(i* something(f)) 

is of course a sin+cos, and maybe an exp if something has an imaginary part.

