> There's a keys/sec benchmark site link on distributed.net's web site.. has
> a whole pile of statistics, and I think it even includes (or links to) a
> bang-for-your-buck page.

In my experience, the Alpha sucks at rc5 cracking.  It's my understanding
that rc5 uses lots of rotate instructions, and the alpha doesn't have a
barrel shifter in it's integer units, where the x86 does.  (My experience
ONLY includes the 21164 and Pentium Pro machines, btw.  The might not be
true with the 21264...)

On the other hand, the Alpha destroys the x86 in cracking DES keys...

(Yet another example of why benchmarks suck.)

