  http://www.fortify.net/


I use it all the time, on RedHat 4.2 or 5.1, kernels 2.0.30 or 2.0.34,
at 500 Mhz or 433 Mhz, various navigator versions etc...


There's a static arena binary:
  ftp://networks.ecse.rpi.edu/pub/stewart/arena-beta-3b-linux_axp


You can use em86 to run amaya:
  http://www.w3c.org/Amaya/User/BinDist.html


Lynx ought to be installed already.


There's a browser in KDE too.


For html on local disk, there's XMayday:
  ftp://ftp.axene.com/pub/xmayday/INDEX.html
  ftp://ftp.axene.com/pub/xmayday/doc/INDEX.html


As for non-working browser's, the choice is vast!  =:-)
The most interesting, mozilla:

  ftp://ftp.lsl.com/pub/mozilla/axp/

crashes almost immediately on start-up :(


