Yes this does happen, but there is a work around.
Run netscape from this shellscript (I have it installed as
/usr/local/bin/netscape, with netscape installed under
/usr/local/netscape). This fix is a slight modification of that released by
Larry Zimmerman, see
http://walleye.gonefishing.sk.ca/laz/linux/netscape.html

#!/bin/sh

MOZILLA_HOME="/usr/local/netscape"

#  check for lock file
if [ -L $HOME/.netscape/lock ]
then
  /usr/sbin/fuser -u $MOZILLA_HOME/netscape | grep -q $LOGNAME  && exit 0
  rm -f $HOME/.netscape/lock
fi
export MOZILLA_HOME
export MOZILLA_NO_ASYNC_DNS=True
exec $MOZILLA_HOME/netscape -no-about-splash $*
exit 0

