>
>That's fairly extraordinary.
>
>At first glance, it feels unbelievable.
>
>Then I think back to the numbers of clock cycles that IA-32 instructions
>can take, and it starts to become conceivable. 
>
>Does this mean that a 200MHz PPC (say a 603) is faster, for this sort of
>thing, by further factors?  I wouldn't necessarily expect an 8x
>improvement over the 25MHz part, but would be interested in hearing how
>it *should* factor... 

No, the chip he's talking about is different from the PowerPC chips.
It is a floating-point beast.

The Power series has a lot in common with the PPC's, but they have
sort of a different emphasis.

Here are some SPEC92 benchmarks....  (the only ones available, apparently,
for the 320H.)



Machine		  CPU	     MHz     cache	 int	  fp
******************************************************************************
IBM 320H          POWER      25      8/64         20.9    39.4  Nov92 Sunflash
IBM 43P           MPC604     133     512+16/16   176.4   156.5  Jun95 www.ibm
Intel Alder       PentPro    200     256+8/8     318.4   283.2  Jan96 www.intel


SPEC92 isn't available for P-II's.  (SPEC92 being obsolete by that time)
Given the sort of performance, I'm of the opinion that the LaPack
was crippled in some way on his 300MHz P-II.  Then again, I know
the memory architecture of the Power machines was something special.

I realize that LaPack and SPECfp92 are rather different, but I'd hope
they'd correlate to within a factor of 3....  (So that a machine 9x faster
than another in SPEC92fp would be at least 3x faster in LaPack....)

It could easily happen that a poor implementation of LaPack could be
10x slower than a good implementation.

Below, for giggles, are the benchmarks for the leading CPU's in the field,
from a few vendors:

Sun Ultra2/2200   2xUltSP    100/200 1M+16/16    332     505    Nov95 SunIntro
SGI PowerChl,Onyx R8000      90      4M+16/16    132.2   396.1  Aug95 SGI Ptabl
IBM 591/R21       POWER2     77      32/256      143.5   307.9  Jul95 www.ibm
HP J210           PA7200     120     256/256     168.7   269.2  Jun95 www.hp
DEC 8[24]00/5/350 A21164     88/350  4M+96+8/8   432.8   602.2  Feb96 Digital

