running RedHat Linux 5.0, not 5.1, so if you do have a 3.3.2 server,
you might want to try running the card only in 8-bpp mode, as Nils
suggested.  The 3.3.2 server rarely locks me up (and only when the
machine's displaying bitmapped images, but I haven't tried it at a
higher color depth), whereas the older 3.3.1-14 server would lock up
on something as innocent as scrolling text.

FYI, I have an AlphaStation 200 4/233 running RedHat Linux 5.0, kernel
version 2.1.103 (at the moment), glibc-2.0.7-7, XFree86-3.3.1-14, and
XF86_S3 version 3.3.2 (unpatched).  The video card is a Diamond
Stealth 64 VRAM with 4 MBytes of VRAM.

