Hi,

> 	Has anyone ever put normal PC RAM in an alpha and had it work?
Yes. Just that it was normal PC RAM from 1994 :> All Alphas I know
/need/ parity, and as they use is somewhat different than PCs do,
it mustn't be an electronically simulated parity. Such RAM is normally
called ECC-RAM (ECC=Error Correction Code) and available at slightly higher
prices than the normal RAM, as it actually is /more/ RAM and less often
demanded. Oh, and I think you should buy Fast-Page RAM. I heard about EDO
RAM working in some machines, but at least in the Multias and other machines
of that age the original RAM isn't EDO.

