We're doing some fairly aggressive coding on our alpha 533 and with our
initial results found that our code didn't go particularly fast so we
started delving into the assembler to see what was happening, now we
know what to do we have gone back to the C code, straightened it out and
recompiled with egs1.03a -O2 and the code is much faster than
previously, approximately twice as fast as it was before.

The lesson from this is even in C you need to be aware of how a
processor and compiler work if you really want your code to cook.  True
for the Pentium too but you have a lot more room to work on an alpha.

