In short: Yes it runs fine on my Noname which is in fact nearly the same
machine.
Longer version:
You should be able to compile Gimp and GTK on your machine without any
problems. But when running you will for sure get something like

 XShm: Access to private resource denied

Which will subsequently cause all other Gimp windows (or subprocesses) to
crash. Reason for this is that RH up to version 5.1 uses the "old" 2.0.*
series of kernels which have a SysV-IPC bug which causes the X11 shared
memory extensions to fail. Even the latest 2.0.34 has this problem (GRRRR!).
