Date: 1998/06/17
Message-ID: <3587D846.B04B8DA7@dirac.phys.uwm.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 363532134
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
References: <35830BCE.19D03F04@dirac.phys.uwm.edu> <feigin.897829131@maipo.ee.ethz.ch>
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: University of Wisconsin - Milwaukee, Physics Department
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha


I have finally gotten a working install on RH5.1 on  my XL300 (XLT).

Significant steps were:

Build MILO disk as follows:
(1) Make a dos formatted floppy.  Build an msdos file system on it.  Mount RedHat
5.1 cd, then
       cp /mnt/cdrom/milo/xlt-alcor /mnt/floppy
       cp /mnt/cdrom/milo/arc/linload.exe   /mnt/floppy/linload.exe

       Note that the /mnt/cdrom/milo/images directory is empty.  Note that the
milo included here is NOT the
       standard distributed one: it reads /etc/milo.conf from the ramdisk floppy.

Build BOOT disk as follows:
(2)  Make a dos formatted floppy.  Then use
        dd if=/mnt/cdrom/images/alcor.img of=/dev/fd0
        to copy the boot image onto the disk.  Note: this creates an ext2
formatted filesystem on the
        disk that contains, in addition to vmlinux.gz, an /etc/milo.conf file on
the floppy!

        The kernel on your boot disk will NOT run properly on an XLT.  Do not use
it!  In addition,
         don't succumb to the temptation of using the mnt/cdrom/images/xlt.img
file, which is
         from Nov 1997 and contains a 2.0.30 kernel.  The bottom line is that the
RH5.1 disk does not
         contain a working kernel for 2.0.34 for an XLT.  You will have to build
this yourself.  To do
         this, download the kernel sources from:

                    http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/

         and build the kernel on a standard RH 4.2-running machine.  Then mount
your boot disk
         [Note: it contains an ext2 not msdos file system!]
         mount /dev/floppy /mnt/floppy
         and copy the new kernel image to it:
         cp /kernel/from/my/own/build/vmlinux.gz /mnt/floppy
         Note: you should follow my procedure because this disk contains other
files besides vmlinux.gz that
         the RH installation procedure requires.

Make the RAMDISK as follows
(3)  make a dos formatted floppy, then use
       dd if=/mnt/cdrom/images/ramdisk.img of=/dev/fd0

Having followed this procedure, just boot from the MILO disk.  You will get a
MILO> prompt.  Then
do :

MILO> boot floppy           [yes, I know this normally won't work but the
MILO you've put on the disk does recognize this]
boot:  linux

and the RH 5.1 installation will procede as normal.

HINT:  you may want to prepare an additional floppy disk containing the "date"
and "clock" commands.
As soon as you get the the first RH5.1 installation screen, use <CONTROL-ALT> F2
to get to the
command line prompt, and use your date and clock commands to set the time
properly so that the file
creation dates are correct.  Then use <CONTROL-ALT> F1 to get back to the RedHat
installation screens.

The only real pain in the ass here is having to build your own working 2.0.34
kernel (the included one generates
huge numbers of device_interrupt errors because the ALCOR interupt request mask
is not the same as the
XLT one -- thanks to Jay Estabrook for help with this.]

Fellow XLT owners: Good luck!

Bruce Allen




