The Pentium II currently holds third place in integer
performance, obviously highly competitive, whereas the
P2SC is weak.
For floating point performance, it is pretty much the
other way round.
(The leading architectures are in both cases Alpha and
PA-8200, but Pentium II and P2SC come close on integer/
floating point performance respectively).
Note,  that Power PC and P2SC are not the same.
Power PC and Pentium II are very similar in performance,
with slight advantage for Pentium on integer, and slight
advantage for Power PC on floating point.
(comparence based on SPECint95b/SPECfp95b).

Jochem



