Subject: Has anyone gotten RH 5.1 to work on an XL300 machine?
Date: 1998/06/13
Message-ID: <35830BCE.19D03F04@dirac.phys.uwm.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 362411447
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: University of Wisconsin - Milwaukee, Physics Department
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha


Hi, I thought that I'd post my very disappointing experiences with RH
5.1.  I recently paid $49 to get a couple of new manuals and CD.
Although I was able to install RH4.2 on my XL300 machines, I was never
able to get RH5.0 to work.  But seeing as many other people had
apparently had the same problems I figured that perhaps RedHat had had a
chance to fix things and that 5.1 would work.

Wanting to have a fresh start, I took a machine and tried doing a clean
install, not upgrade, carefully following the directions in the new
RedHat 5.1 Alpha Installation Addendum manual.

As instructed, I formatted 3 MSDOS disks, and used dd to copy from the
CDROM:
1. The ramdisk (this went fine)
2. The boot image.
     Oops!  Here was the first (perhaps) sign of trouble.  I took the
alcor boot image as instructed, from the images/
     directory of the CD-ROM, but curiously, there was ANOTHER boot
image in there, ominously labeled xlt
     The alcor image was dated May 11, 98 but the xlt image was from
1997.
3  The milo image.  Here, according to the instructions, I was supposed
to copy the appropriate image from
      milo/images.  But milo/images was EMPTY: not a single file in that
directory.  Sweating now, I copied
      the xlt-alcor image from milo.

In fact, something is not right with that milo image.  I could not mount
the disk as an msdos file system on another
machine.

Next problem:  the boot instructions in the new RedHat 5.1 Alpha
Installation Addendum manual give instructions
for booting from the ARC console, but not from AlphaBios.  OK, well I've
been there before.... so I put in the correct
commands so that linload.exe would load MILO.

Next problem: the boot instructions in the new RedHat 5.1 Alpha
Installation Addendum manual now say to give the
MILO command:
    boot floppy
Of course this doesn't work -- but I knew to type
   boot fd0:vmlinux.gz load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1
which did work.   The new kernel loaded and unzipped nicely, but the
moment that it started kswapd all hell broke loose
and the screen was covered with:

device_interrupt: unexpected device interupt N

where N is a number between 1 and 30.  At this point, this being a
Saturday, and having better ways to enjoy
myself, I decided in disgust that RedHat 5.1 is probably about as much a
piece of junk as 5.0 was.

[By the way, to confirm that this was not some new and unexpected
hardware problem, I repeated this on another
machine, and it failed in exactly the same way.]  And yes, I do have the
latest correct version of MILO.

Could anyone correct this impression?  Has anyone been able to (a)
follow the delivered instructions or
(b) find some variation that works on an XL300 (XLT) machine?

Cheers,
    Bruce Allen


  milo/im




