I dont have the instructions, but I used my intuition and mapped the 5.0
addendum, and was able to get my XL300 up and running last weekend. It also
helped that I installed a 53c875 controller and 9GB UW disk, and installed
5.1 onto that; leaving my 5.0 installation on the Quantum 2GB untouched.

Suggestion:

Make an entry in your Alphabios that just boots up MILO, without attempting to
then boot the kernel; (i.e. you're at the MILO prompt). Then, take your
boot and ramdisk floppies (discard your milo floppy, you dont need it!), and
run the boot floppy command. Definietly use the xlt.img that is in the images
directory; forget about the alcor (perhaps its a typo in the 5.1 Addendum ?).
You'll then get prompted for the ramdisk floppy, and the installation should
proceed as normal.

I didn't have any major problems with the install; just some bizzare install
times for certain packages (did an installation over NFS). The whole thing
took about 1/2 hour.

I couldn't get my previously installed egcs (1.0.3a, later than the one in
the distribution) for compile the 2.0.34 kernel correctly, although the
distribution one had no problem; I used 1.0.3a to compile 2.1.105, and had
no problems.

Hope this helps.

