hey... i was there. i know.  ok, at this point y'all have two options...
you can leave mr. well_enough alone, and boot from srm, or you can
update your firmware and boot from milo.  i am having a bear of a time
getting milo to work, but i can see that once i figure out what debian's
fdisk program is and how to use it, milo is the way to go.  however, to
boot from floppy in srm, do the following:(from the srm prompt >>>)boot
dva0 -file vmlinux.gz -flags"root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1
prompt_ramdisk=1" and it will start up.  now, once you have linux
installed, in the -flags switch, change "root=/dev/fd0..." to
"root=/dev/sda1..." sda1 is the first partition on a scsi hdd, change
the number to whereever you installed the root.  to do the milo thing,
go to http://www.mindspring.com/~ccsf-lug/AS200.htm and follow his
instructions TO THE LETTER.  and once you figure out how to use debians
fdisk (cuz it will not work otherwise) let me know :)
