Sorry, but I just said what I felt and it was directed as a broad statement.
I'm tired of having to convince people (and these are recent conversations)
that the PII 333MHz doesn't beat an Alpha 21164 600MHz in fp operations.
That yes, my Alpha 21164SX 533MHz (for ~$2000) does beat your dual PII
333MHz (for ~$5000) on this molecular dynamics program.  Or talking to a
Corel rep when I was trying to order WP Suite 8 for Alpha and having to
explain that yes they do have WP Suite 8 for Alpha, that an Alpha is a
processor, no it isn't like a Pentium, and why I bought it instead of the
"faster" systems from Intel.

Anyway, I just think that most of this is because Intel marketing is better
than Alpha Powered's marketing.  So let's hope that Alpha Systems, Inc. will
do a better job in the future.

Mark





