There have now been several reports on the Web about:

device_interrupt: unexpected interrupt N

where in my case N=30 to 35, but other people see different values.
The people seeing these errors are typically using a RedHat 5.1 2.0.34
kernel for the first time.  Reports of this error come from:

Robert Harley <harley@corton.inria.fr>
          Message-ID     <rz7yav5cn9v.fsf@corton.inria.fr>

peterm@tesla.EECS.Berkeley.EDU (Peter Mardahl)
          Message-ID     <6lmfmp$dt9$1@tesla.EECS.Berkeley.EDU

Bruce Allen <ballen@dirac.phys.uwm.edu>
          Message-ID: <35848DE8.89EA6C7E@dirac.phys.uwm.edu>

-------------------------------------------------------------------

In my case, I have a stock XL300 DEC alpha machine, with a DE500
ethernet
board added in.  Other people have different hardware (alpha) setups.

I have a couple of questions for the experts.

(1) The error message is coming from the file:
    /usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/kernel/irq.c

    In the case of 2.0.30 (which does not exhibit the problem) the
relevant lines
    of irq.c read:
-------------------------------------------------------------------
 action = irq_action[irq];
 mask_irq(ack);
 ack_irq(ack);
 if (!action) {
#if 0
