I am quite new to the alpha. So, for what it's worth, I use a two
step boot process. First boot MILO from SRM with the command [boot dva0]
then when you get the MILO> prompt boot redhat with the command
[boot fd:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1]

Good luck,
-tom



