With my system (533mhw LX w/ Adaptec 2940UW) I have had problems with
the Linux driver being able to correctly init when my SCSI CD rom (Sony
slim SCSI model) is active on the chain.  When I turn the player off the
driver (for both Milo and again after booting the kernel) is able to
init the rest of the chain.  This problem does not exist on NT so is
definitely a Linux/Alpha driver issue.  I haven't seen any data/file
sytem corruption yet but haven't really maxed out the drive much in
Linux.

