In article <667ce$f1333.261@XAVIER>,
George Nimmer <george@newtower2-716.resnet.drexel.edu> wrote:
>I'm currently using a Dual Pentium system and am considering upgrading
>to a Alpha in the next few months.  I'm wondering if someone can point me
>to some information on what Alpha hardware are supported by Linux.
>
>Thanks,

PC164, PC164LX, PC164SX motherboards are certainly supported.
These are what you're most likely interested in.
Most of the single-CPU 21164 alphas available directly from DEC are
also supported.

PC164UX and PC164BX motherboards from samsung are probably supported,
you'll want to do some more research.

A lot of older single-CPU alphas are also supported,
though NOT any of the DEC 3000/xxx (Turbochannel) machines.

From what I know, NONE of the multi-CPU DEC's are really supported
by Linux.

This is the location of the FAQ:
http://www.redhat.com/linux-info/alpha/faq/

It seems to be out-of-date, since I know for certain that the LX
and SX motherboards are supported, yet they are not mentioned.

These guys sell Linux/Alpha machines:
www.dcginc.com
www.microway.com
www.aspsys.com
www.swt.com
www.aslab.com
www.linux-hw.com

PeterM



