Hi,

I made fast dgemm routine.  It's a little bit faster than before.
And also includes C version dgemm routine.

  C :=  alpha * A x B  + beta * C

 double a[m][k],  b[k][n], c[m][n];
 double alpha, beta

We can call easily like Fortran dgemm routine.

  dgemm("Non Transpose", "Non Transpose", m, n, k,
         alpha, a, lda, b, ldb, beta, c, ldc);
                   ~~~<- sizeof(a[m])

Of course, Transposed routine is also available and fast.

This routine works both Linux/Alpha and Digital UNIX.
