Not very well.  I have it, with some patches[1], and it has a mean up-time of
about 35 seconds before core dumping.

[1] Attempts to fix some of the egregiously bad, non-64 bit clean code.  But
there is just too much of it - the Netscape developers assumed that a pointer
and an int were interchangable.  Note that even on Digital Unix, the release
versions of Netscape were compiled with a flag that causes it to only use 31
bits for pointers rather than fixing their stupidly broken code.

