>>>>> "TD" == Tony D'Andrade <blue@visinet.ca> writes:

    TD> Hello, I am trying to install RedHat on an Aspen Alpine
    TD> System.

Whee!!

    TD> Does this mean i need two disks ??? One for MILO and one for
    TD> the .img and ramdisk?

If you're booting completely from floppies you need THREE disks: MILO,
the appropriate kernel image, and the ramdisk.  (Since MILO must be on
a DOS-formatted disk, you can just copy `MILO' and `LINLOAD.EXE' from
the MILO floppy to the ARC boot partition and run it from the hard
disk.  You'll probably want to do that later anyway when you go to set
up an automatic boot.)

    TD> If i do need two disks do i have to boot with the MILO disk
    TD> first and once MILO is loaded do i have to switch disks ??

Yup.  Start with the MILO disk in the floppy drive.  You'll select
`Start MILO' (or whatever) from the ARC boot menu and ARC will proceed
to run linload from the floppy.  That will start you up into MILO;
MILO should display a prompt.

Switch disks & put the kernel boot disk in.  Now execute the command
`boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1'
and hit Enter.  The kernel will now be loaded.

If all goes well, you will be prompted for the ramdisk.  Switch disks
again & put the ramdisk in and hit Enter.  The RedHat installer should
then load and all should be well.

    TD> Also the manual says i need to use loadlin.exe on the boot
    TD> disk along with the MILO image. However loadlin.exe is not on
    TD> my CD.  Where do i get loadlin.exe ?? I have searched
    TD> http://www.redhat.com and found nothing.

Well, the program is called `LINLOAD.EXE', not `LOADLIN.EXE' (that's a
DOS program that can boot Linux kernels for systems that use the
umsdos file system), so that might be your problem right there.
Otherwise, `LINLOAD.EXE' is included on the MILO diskette (which is
DOS-formatted, so you should be able to read it in NT or something).

