: For some reason the Linux partitioning
: programs are incompatible with Digital UNIX and BSD (dunno why).

They are compatible if used in that way (and peeking into documentation
definitely helps with understanding).  The other way is compatible
with partitioning used by MS-DOS (all these Intel machines) and NT.
If you want to use on your Alpha DU, Linux and NT then you need at
least two disks and Linux can live on one or another.  DU does not
understand a partitioning scheme used by NT and vice-versa.

