up to 512 Mbytes of industry standard memory".  This suggests that it
can
take up to 64 Mbyte simms.

We've sucessfully tried these memory combinaations:

 4 x 8  Mbytes + 4 x 32 Mbytes = 160 Mbytes
 4 x 32 Mbytes + 4 x 32 Mbytes = 256 Mbytes

[these are all true parity 60 nsec simms].  The following combinations
however fails:

 4 x 32 Mbytes + 4 x 64 Mbytes = 384 Mbytes

The machine beeps 1-2-4 (SROM or memory error) and never makes it to
the firmware screen.  These simms are true parity, 60 nsec

Could anyone confirm from experience if these machines can or can not
in fact use 64 Mbyte simms?  It seems that they can't...

Cheers,
