You should not use the first partition. It is for aboot, the boot
loader,
if you want to boot the OS from Hard Disk.
For example, below is my hard disk partition:

FDISK display (with b option).

/dev/sda
#	size	offset		fstype		Cylinder
a:    224910	32130		swap		3 - 16
b:    257040	257040		ext2		17 - 32
c:   3598560    514080		ext2		33 - 256

As you can see, I begin the first partition from Cylinder 3 ,
and not using cylinder 0,1,2.

And then, install the aboot-0.5-2 RPM package.
And then, write the boot strapper to the Hard disk :

# /sbin/swriteboot /dev/sda /boot/bootlx /vmlinux-2.0.32.gz

Oh, you could refer to the SRM-How To , for more help:
http://www.azstarnet.com/~axplinux/srm.html

engel.



