Congrats.

> I would like to install Windows 95 but I can't get into Linux 
> without a Login and Password. 

That helps nothing. You needn't get logged to the machine for 
installing Win95.

> Unfortunately, the person who donated us the machine has
> moved.  Can anyone help us?

(1)	Take an empty 3.5" floppy and go to somebody with a working
	Win95 system.
(2)	Open a DOS-Prompt on this machine, put your floppy into A:
	and type: FORMAT A: /S
(3)	open explorer and go to the directory c:\windows\command,
	copy the files FDISK FORMAT SYS and MSCDEX to A:
(4)	locate the ATAPI-CDROM driver on his machine (ask him) and
	copy it to A: 
(5) 	go back to the donated machine and switch it off. Insert the
	floppy to a and switch on. Wait
(6)	if it shows "starting Win95", type FDISK  /Y C:\
	and answer all questions with Y - if NOT, mail me for
	further help
(7)	after finishing reset or switch off/on the computer, leave
	the floppy in A:
(8)	type FORMAT C: /S and wait
(9)	after finishing (Pressing Enter and stuff), remove the
	disk from a and reboot (alt ctrl del)

OK if all that works, you are very close. Mail me for further hints
if necessary.

Mirco



